# Compare Social Attention With Motion Baselines

Evaluate the trained flat dense triplet model and three deterministic predictors on
the same held-out MABe windows. Every method observes 8 frames and predicts the
next 12 frames. Ground-truth motion tertiles define the low-, medium-, and
high-motion slices once and are shared by all methods.

| Method | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Persistence | Repeats the final observed pose. |
| Rigid constant velocity | Translates the final pose using centroid velocity. |
| Keypoint constant velocity | Extrapolates every keypoint independently. |
| Social Attention | Samples autoregressively from `flat_best.pt`. |

## Run the fair comparison

This inference-only cell evaluates 1,000 windows with seed 42, prints Rich tables
for the overall distribution and each motion slice, and appends one combined
record to `outputs/evaluations/flat_dense_triplet_30fps/benchmark_8_12/results.jsonl`.
Values in parentheses are relative error improvements over persistence: positive
is better, negative is worse, and blank means the reference is undefined or zero.

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
import os
from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src").exists())
os.environ.setdefault("MPLCONFIGDIR", str(repo_root / "outputs/matplotlib"))
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from benchmark import load_benchmark_config, print_benchmark_tables, run_benchmark

config = load_benchmark_config(repo_root / "src/config/benchmark__flat_dense_triplet_30fps.yml")
record = run_benchmark(config)
print_benchmark_tables(record)
```

## CLI equivalent

Run the same comparison from the repository root:

```sh
python src/benchmark.py --config src/config/benchmark__flat_dense_triplet_30fps.yml
```

## Reading the result

Use trajectory metrics (`centroid_*`, `keypoint_*`) to judge spatial prediction,
`CVE`/`KVE` velocity errors to judge first-derivative motion, pose and structure
metrics to diagnose body fidelity, and ordering metrics to detect keypoint
inversions. Do not combine these into one score.

The primary question is whether Social Attention improves over persistence in
the medium- and high-motion slices. Strong aggregate performance without those
improvements would mean that low-motion windows are masking model failure.

## Recorded result

Snapshot recorded on 2026-09-12 in
`outputs/evaluations/flat_dense_triplet_30fps/benchmark_8_12/results.jsonl`. At that time,
`flat_best.pt` resolved to epoch 45 with validation loss -6.962924 and was
evaluated on 1,000 windows. These aggregate metrics are all lower-is-better:

| Method | cADE px | cFDE px | kADE px | kFDE px | BHE deg | BLE px | ROE |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Persistence | 6.615 | 11.183 | 8.321 | 13.687 | 7.136 | 3.658 | 0.068 |
| Rigid constant velocity | 6.602 | 12.126 | 8.394 | 14.592 | 7.136 | 3.658 | 0.069 |
| Keypoint constant velocity | 6.602 | 12.126 | 9.962 | 17.775 | 9.091 | 7.201 | 0.089 |
| Social Attention | 32.277 | 55.358 | 38.891 | 62.468 | 31.931 | 19.060 | 0.248 |

Centroid FDE exposes how the comparison changes with ground-truth motion:

| Motion slice | Persistence | Rigid CV | Keypoint CV | Social Attention |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Low | 1.379 px | 3.516 px | 3.516 px | 54.516 px |
| Medium | 4.789 px | 8.823 px | 8.823 px | 49.866 px |
| High | 27.411 px | 24.063 px | 24.063 px | 61.694 px |

The trained model does not beat persistence in any slice. Its overall centroid
FDE is 395.0% worse and keypoint FDE is 356.4% worse than persistence. Rigid
constant velocity only becomes useful in the high-motion slice, where centroid
FDE improves by 12.2% over persistence. The learned result is one seeded
Gaussian rollout per window, so future uncertainty experiments should repeat
sampling or report best-of-N separately rather than mixing that question into
this baseline comparison.
